Phase 2a of batch 8 on the family card: the thirty (iii) node type keys leave the registry. Implemented by `os-dev` for `domain:ui` seat 1, session `session_01YLg8XqWGJ785fwQ5v4pH37`. Claim `5945225235`, phase-1 report `5945491717`, binding seat ruling `5945530142`.

## The ruling this implements

The seat ruling `5945530142`, "Phase 2a: the 30 (iii) keys (one `Part of` PR)", under mechanism M1 route A, which adds no new instrument:

- **The 28 bare field-widget fallbacks are retired through `skipFallback`.** The keys are `auto_number` `boolean` `checkboxes` `color` `currency` `date` `datetime` `file` `formula` `geolocation` `location` `lookup` `master_detail` `multiselect` `number` `object` `percent` `phone` `qrcode` `radio` `rating` `richtext` `signature` `summary` `tags` `url` `user` `vector`.
  - They join `FIELD_TYPES_SKIP_FALLBACK` in `packages/fields/src/index.tsx`, so each widget now registers only `field:TYPE`.
  - `field:TYPE` is the only key a form ever looked up (`renderFieldComponent`, ruling B of objectui#5254).
  - The set now holds every key of `fieldWidgetMap`. Its docblock says so, and says why no key may come back out.
- **`tree` and `view` are unregistered.** They were aliases of the armed `object-tree` / `object-view`, with no node producers. Each keeps a tombstone docblock in the objectui#10393 / objectui#8760 form. Removed with them:
  - the console's lazy `tree` stub;
  - the `tree` / `view:tree` rows of `@object-ui/core`'s record-source `data` arm table;
  - the `view` rows of the plugin-view README table and the `plugin-view.mdx` registration table.

  The plugin-tree README now registers one type. The component-registry guide's built-ins lists named `tree`; they now name `tree-view`, the tree `@object-ui/components` registers.
- **The doc gate is handled by M2 option A, on the objectui#8802 precedent.** `check:doc-types` judges every fenced `type` value against the same derived universe, and it cannot tell a field type from a node type. Those values passed only because the bare fallback shared their spelling. 53 per-file `DOC_TYPE_EXEMPTIONS` rows now declare them. They cover 116 sites in 35 files, and each row names its vocabulary and its declaration:
  - field pages: the page's `XFieldMetadata` (`FieldMetadata`), rendered by `field:TYPE`;
  - grid-field columns: `GridFieldMetadata.columns`, from the spec's `FieldSchema.inlineColumns`;
  - list columns: `ListColumnSchema.type`;
  - object-definition fields: the spec's `FieldType`;
  - report field types and section kinds: `ReportField.type`, `ReportSection.type`, `ReportSchema` kinds;
  - nested JSON Schema property types in `object` fields;
  - navigation item kinds: `NavigationItemType`;
  - action parameters: `ActionParam`;
  - designer input kinds: `ComponentInput.type`;
  - the component-registry walkthrough, which registers its own `rating` key.

  The `fieldWidgetMap` entry's reason in `scripts/check-doc-component-types.mjs` now states the new state.

## Ratchet movement

| pin | before | after | what moved |
|:--|:--|:--|:--|
| `REFUSED_AT_TYPE` (bare) | 66 | **36** | the 28 field fallbacks, plus `tree` and `view` |
| `NAMESPACED_REFUSED_AT_TYPE` (objectui#10872's pin) | 391 | **389** | `view:tree` and `plugin-view:view`, the twins of the two unregistered aliases |

`packages/cli/src/utils/known-schema-types.ts` is regenerated by its script. The net change is 32 deletions: the 30 bare keys and the 2 namespaced twins.

The ratchet file now names the thirty keys (`RETIRED_BARE_KEYS_10859_BATCH_8`) in one appended row. That row asserts four things:
- the thirty keys are gone from the population;
- they are still refused at `type`, because no arm was added;
- every `field:TYPE` key is still registered;
- `object-tree` / `object-view` are still present.

The non-vacuity floor on the bare population goes from 200 to 150, because 199 bare keys remain; a comment records why. ⛔ Neither pin rises.

## Tests and pins re-pointed

Each of these pinned a retired key:
- the `registry-collision` row is inverted: no field type populates a bare fallback, with a lit control on the bare keys `@object-ui/components` owns;
- the plugin-tree public-tier, inputs and data-arm pins;
- the `objectViewHostSurface` alias row;
- the react record-source mirror lists (objectui#9571 / objectui#9758);
- the `check-schema-marker` JSON-Schema row: the one false positive of objectui#6075's discriminator is gone, because `object` is no longer registered;
- the html-tier census ledger, which carried `summary`, `object` and `view` as bare registrations squatting on element names.

Three pending changesets described the `tree` alias in the present tense (11168, 8348, 10064). Each gains a dated note, and its frontmatter is byte-identical.

## Changesets

One changeset per released package whose code moved. Each is `minor` with a BREAKING (authoring) banner and a migration line per retired spelling, on the objectui#8760 precedent:
- `@object-ui/fields`: 28 migration lines;
- `@object-ui/plugin-tree`;
- `@object-ui/plugin-view`;
- `@object-ui/cli` (the regenerated list);
- `@object-ui/core` (the record-source rows);
- `@object-ui/console` (the lazy stub).

`@object-ui/react` changed test files only, so it carries no entry (the objectui#10393 precedent).

